    {"s": "Modern History", "c": "Advent of Europeans", "q": "During whose reign did the East India Company establish their first factory in India?", "o": ["Jahangir", "Shahjahan", "Aurangzeb", "Bahadur Shah-I"], "a": 0, "e": "The English East India Company established its first factory in India (at Surat / Masulipatnam) during the reign of Mughal Emperor Jahangir."},
    {"s": "Environmental Studies", "c": "Air Pollution & Plant Physiology", "q": "Which pollutant of the atmosphere inhibits the Hill reaction of photosynthesis?", "o": ["Peroxyacetyl nitrate (PAN)", "Nitrogen monoxide", "Ultra violet rays", "Hydrocarbon"], "a": 0, "e": "Peroxyacetyl nitrate (PAN), a major secondary photochemical smog pollutant, strongly inhibits the Hill reaction (photolysis of water and electron transport) in chloroplasts."},
    {"s": "Indian Economy", "c": "Industrial Growth", "q": "Which of the following industries has shown a high rate of growth since the 1980s?", "o": ["Capital goods industries", "Intermediate goods industries", "Consumer durable goods industries", "Consumer non-durable goods industries"], "a": 2, "e": "Driven by rising middle-class incomes and liberalization since the 1980s, consumer durable goods industries recorded the fastest growth rate among industrial segments."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Set Theory & Percentages", "q": "In an examination 40% students fail in English, 30% in Mathematics and 15% in both. Then the pass percentage is", "o": ["50%", "30%", "65%", "45%"], "a": 3, "e": "Failed in at least one subject = 40% + 30% - 15% = 55%. Students who passed in both = 100% - 55% = 45%."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Linear Equations & Arithmetic", "q": "2 oranges, 3 bananas and 4 apples taken together cost Rs. 15.00. 3 oranges, 2 bananas and 1 apple cost Rs. 10.00. Then the cost of 3 oranges, 3 bananas and 3 apples is", "o": ["Rs. 12.00", "Rs. 16.00", "Rs. 20.00", "Rs. 15.00"], "a": 3, "e": "Add the two equations: (2O + 3B + 4A) + (3O + 2B + 1A) = 15 + 10 => 5O + 5B + 5A = 25 => O + B + A = 5. Multiply by 3: 3O + 3B + 3A = Rs. 15.00."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Geometry & Triangles", "q": "Which of the triangles with the measures of sides given below is an obtuse-angled triangle?", "o": ["(12, 5, 13) cm", "(6, 7, 5) cm", "(7, 3, 5) cm", "(8, 8, 8) cm"], "a": 2, "e": "A triangle with sides a <= b < c is obtuse-angled if a^2 + b^2 < c^2. For (3, 5, 7): 3^2 + 5^2 = 9 + 25 = 34 < 7^2 (49), so it is obtuse-angled! ((5,12,13) is right-angled; (5,6,7) and (8,8,8) are acute)."},
    {"s": "Medieval History", "c": "Delhi Sultanate", "q": "Which Sultan of Delhi brought one Asokan Pillar to Delhi?", "o": ["Iltutmish", "Alauddin Khilji", "Md. Bin Tughlaq", "Firuz Shah Tughlaq"], "a": 3, "e": "Sultan Firuz Shah Tughlaq transported two Ashokan sandstone pillars—one from Topra (Ambala) and one from Meerut—and re-erected them in Delhi."},
    {"s": "Indian Polity", "c": "Seventh Schedule", "q": "Which of the following items comes under the concurrent list?", "o": ["Agriculture", "Labour Welfare", "Public Health", "Insurance"], "a": 1, "e": "Welfare of labour (Entry 24) is placed in the Concurrent List (Agriculture and Public Health are in the State List; Insurance is in the Union List)."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Mensuration & Algebra", "q": "A rectangular field is half as wide as it is long, and its perimeter is p. The area of the field is", "o": ["p^2 / 2", "2p^2", "p^2 / 18", "2p^2 / 9"], "a": 2, "e": "Let length = L and width = L/2. Perimeter p = 2(L + L/2) = 3L => L = p/3, and width = p/6. Area = (p/3) * (p/6) = p^2 / 18."},
    {"s": "Modern History", "c": "British Expansion & Policies", "q": "The policy of Subsidiary Alliance was introduced by", "o": ["Dalhousie", "Canning", "Wellesley", "Warren Hastings"], "a": 2, "e": "Lord Wellesley introduced the Subsidiary Alliance system in 1798."},
    {"s": "Modern History", "c": "Socio-Political Organizations", "q": "\"The Servants of India\" Society was founded by", "o": ["M. N. Joshi", "H. N. Kunzru", "B. G. Tilak", "G. K. Gokhale"], "a": 3, "e": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale founded the Servants of India Society in 1905 (note: in the printed paper, V. D. Savarkar was printed in D while Gokhale is the authentic founder; Option D / Gokhale is the standard question)."},
    {"s": "Current Affairs", "c": "Sports", "q": "Which of the following teams won the 58th National Volleyball Championship Tournament held in January, 2010?", "o": ["Karnataka", "West Bengal", "Tamil Nadu", "Kerala"], "a": 2, "e": "Tamil Nadu won the men’s title at the 58th Senior National Volleyball Championship in January 2010."},
    {"s": "Medieval History", "c": "Conquest of Bengal", "q": "Which Muslim invader conquered Bengal during the time of Lakshmanasena?", "o": ["Muhammad Ghori", "Bakhtiyar Khilji", "Qutbuddin Aibak", "Iltutmish"], "a": 1, "e": "Ikhtiyar-ud-din Muhammad bin Bakhtiyar Khalji invaded Nabadwip and conquered Bengal around 1204 CE during the reign of King Lakshmana Sena."},
    {"s": "Modern History", "c": "Socio-Religious & Cultural Movements", "q": "Who was the main inspiration of the Young Bengal movement?", "o": ["Raja Rammohan Roy", "L. V. Derozio", "Debendranath Tagore", "David Hare"], "a": 1, "e": "Henry Louis Vivian Derozio inspired and mentored the Young Bengal Movement at Hindu College."},
    {"s": "Indian National Movement", "c": "Simon Commission", "q": "Why were the Indians dissatisfied with the Simon Commission?", "o": ["Because no Indian was taken as a member of the Commission.", "Because Indians never wanted the review of the working of Act of 1919.", "Because it recommended that Dyarchy in the provinces should be abolished.", "None of the above"], "a": 0, "e": "Indians universally boycotted the all-white Simon Commission because not a single Indian was included among its seven members."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Cube Cutting & Mensuration", "q": "27 cubes of equal size have been placed in a way to form a single large cube. Then how many cubes will not be visible at all?", "o": ["3", "4", "2", "1"], "a": 3, "e": "27 = 3^3, so n = 3. The number of inner hidden cubes not visible on any exterior face = (n - 2)^3 = (3 - 2)^3 = 1^3 = 1."},
    {"s": "Biology", "c": "Plant Cell & Biomolecules", "q": "Essential constituent of plant cell wall is the carbohydrate,", "o": ["Cellulose", "Sucrose", "Starch", "Lignin"], "a": 0, "e": "Cellulose, a structural polysaccharide of beta-D-glucose, is the primary essential constituent of plant cell walls."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Age Problems", "q": "Mr. X has four children. His age equals to the sum of the ages of his four children. After 20 years his age will be one half of his children's combined age. Mr. X's present age is", "o": ["40 years", "56 years", "66 years", "70 years"], "a": 0, "e": "Let Mr. X's present age = x = sum of 4 children's ages. After 20 years: Mr. X's age = x + 20, and combined age of 4 children = x + 4(20) = x + 80. Given: x + 20 = 1/2 * (x + 80) => 2x + 40 = x + 80 => x = 40 years."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Mathematical Operations", "q": "If 4 c 3 d 8 a 10 b 5 = 18, where a, b, c, d stand for four fundamental arithmetical operations of addition, subtraction, multiplication and division, but not necessarily in this order, then the value of 3 c 4 a 2 d 6 b 3 is", "o": ["3", "9", "10", "12"], "a": 2, "e": "Testing operators in 4 c 3 d 8 a 10 b 5 = 18: let c = ×, d = +, a = -, b = ÷. Check: (4 × 3) + 8 - (10 ÷ 5) = 12 + 8 - 2 = 18 (valid!). Apply same mapping to 3 c 4 a 2 d 6 b 3: (3 × 4) - 2 + (6 ÷ 3) = 12 - 2 + 2 = 12... Wait: let us check both valid permutations! If c = ×, d = -, a = +, b = ÷: (4 × 3) - 8 + (10 ÷ 5) = 12 - 8 + 2 = 6 != 18. If c = +, d = ×, a = -, b = ÷: 4 + (3 × 8) - (10 ÷ 5) = 4 + 24 - 2 = 26 != 18. What if c = ×, d = +, a = -, b = ÷: 3×4 - 2 + 6÷3 = 12 - 2 + 2 = 12 (Option D)! What if c = +, d = ×, a = ÷, b = -: 4 + 3×8 ÷ 10 - 5 (not integer). What if c = ×, d = -, a = ÷, b = +: 4×3 - 8÷10 + 5 (not integer). Thus c=×, d=+, a=-, b=÷ is the unique integer solution, giving 12 (Option D)."},
    {"s": "Indian National Movement", "c": "Jallianwala Bagh Massacre", "q": "Jallianwala Bagh Massacre took place in the year", "o": ["1914", "1916", "1919", "1929"], "a": 2, "e": "The Jallianwala Bagh massacre occurred on 13 April 1919."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Profit and Loss", "q": "A dealer sold a radio for Rs. 540 losing 10%. At what price should he have sold to earn a 10% profit?", "o": ["Rs. 660", "Rs. 650", "Rs. 600", "None of the above"], "a": 0, "e": "Cost Price CP = 540 / 0.90 = Rs. 600. Selling price for 10% profit = 600 * 1.10 = Rs. 660."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Linear Equations & Algebra", "q": "If 15 apples and 20 oranges cost as much as 20 apples and 15 oranges, then which of the following conclusions is correct?", "o": ["Orange and apple have equal price", "Orange is costlier", "Apple is costlier", "No conclusion can be made"], "a": 0, "e": "15A + 20O = 20A + 15O => 5O = 5A => O = A. Thus oranges and apples have equal price."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Number Series", "q": "The next term of the series 30, 42, 56, 72, .... is", "o": ["84", "88", "90", "92"], "a": 2, "e": "Pattern n*(n+1): 5*6=30, 6*7=42, 7*8=56, 8*9=72, 9*10=90."},
    {"s": "World & Physical Geography", "c": "Latitudes & Longitudes", "q": "The latitude of a place is expressed by its angular distance in relation to", "o": ["South Pole", "North Pole", "Equator", "Axis of the Earth"], "a": 2, "e": "Latitude measures the angular distance north or south of the Earth’s Equator (0° latitude)."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Inequalities & Logic", "q": "P, Q, R, S are four positive numbers satisfying the condition P + Q > R + S, Q > S, P + R = Q, P + S = Q + R. Then the least and greatest numbers are", "o": ["P, Q", "R, Q", "P, S", "S, P"], "a": 1, "e": "Add P + R = Q and P + S = Q + R: 2P + R + S = 2Q + R => 2P + S = 2Q => Q - P = S/2 > 0 => Q > P. Also P + R = Q => Q > R. From P + S = Q + R and Q > P, we get S > R. And P + Q > R + S with Q = P + R gives 2P + R > R + S => 2P > S, while Q = P + S/2 > S/2 + P > S => Q is greatest and R is least! Thus (R, Q) is the pair of least and greatest numbers."},
    {"s": "General Mental Ability", "c": "Mensuration & Percentages", "q": "If the radius of a circle is increased by 100%, then the area of the circle will be increased by", "o": ["100%", "200%", "300%", "400%"], "a": 2, "e": "If radius r increases by 100%, new radius r' = 2r. Area A' = pi * (2r)^2 = 4 * pi * r^2 = 4A. Percentage increase = (4A - A) / A * 100 = 300%."},
    {"s": "Indian Economy", "c": "Five-Year Plans", "q": "What was the revised target rate of growth in the 11th Plan?", "o": ["8 percent", "8.5 percent", "9 percent", "8.1 percent"], "a": 3, "e": "The Eleventh Five-Year Plan (2007–2012) initially targeted 9% GDP growth, which was later revised to 8.1% following the global financial crisis."}
